# RUN: llc -mtriple=mncore2 %s -o - | FileCheck %s
#
# G2 tripwire: gpfn3's `fmfma` does not evaluate the A*x product.
#
# This is deliberately NOT a numeric golden for the MAU product. It pins a
# measured negative result (design doc section 22.9) so that a change in the
# emulator is detected instead of silently invalidating the G2 conclusion:
#
#   A rows 0..3 = BF(1.0), x = 4 x BF(1.0), y = 0x40C00000
#   SDM 3.6.9.4 predicts dst = 1+1+1+1 + 6.0 = 10.0 -> 0x41200000
#     (fmfma's addend and result are plain IEEE f32, not block float; the
#      vendor header mncl/device/mncore2.h documents that, design doc 22.10)
#   measured:           dst == y bit for bit       -> 0x40C00000
#
# scripts/check_mau_g2.py exits non-zero when the measured pattern stops
# holding, i.e. when the emulator starts computing the product. At that point
# G2 can be closed for real and this file must become a golden.
#
# Face, operand spaces, mat immediate and latency were all varied with no
# effect (section 22.9.2); this fixture keeps the canonical X-face form.

--- |
  target triple = "mncore2"
  define void @mau_g2() { ret void }
...
---
